    "gitCommitMessage": "Fix piano keyboard + add penguin-guided chord library (#3)\n\n* Fix piano keyboard: real multi-touch polyphony, reliable sound + haptics\n\nThe on-screen keyboard rendered one <Pressable> per key in an absolute-\npositioned overlay. React Native's gesture-responder system only grants the\nactive responder to one or two overlapping views at a time, which caused the\nreported bugs:\n  - couldn't sound more than ~2 notes at once, so chords were impossible\n  - many keys (notably the black keys overlapping the white tap targets) never\n    fired their press handler -> no sound AND no haptic on those keys\n  - constant responder hand-off between dozens of Pressables made the keyboard\n    feel laggy/buggy\n\nReplace the per-key Pressable overlay with a single touch surface\n(pointerEvents=\"box-only\") that reads every active finger from\nnativeEvent.touches and hit-tests each one to a key (black keys win the upper\nregion, white keys below). This gives true polyphony, glissando, and a\nreliable tap -> sound + haptic on every white and black key.\n\nPublic props, the audio engine, and the SVG rendering (LED strip, octave\nlabels, lit-note glow) are all unchanged.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01J4JRpRUmttWRgFiWVUpbMk\n\n* Practice tab: penguin-guided chord library with full chord tree\n\nReplaces the 4 hard-coded demo chips with a complete, browsable chord library\non the Practice tab, guided by Maestro Penguini (the same mascot used in\nlessons). It uses the multi-touch keyboard fixed earlier, so picked chords\nlight up and every key plays/buzzes.\n\nFlow (the \"music tree\"):\n  1. Pick a root letter (C D E F G A B).\n  2. Pick the accidental (b / natural / #) and the chord quality.\n  3. The chord lights on the keyboard, rolls out so each note is heard, and\n     the penguin explains its notes + character. Tap the lit keys to play it\n     yourself.\n\nNew src/music/chords.ts holds every common chord grouped into a theory tree:\n  - Triads: maj, min, dim, aug, sus2, sus4, power\n  - Sixths: 6, m6\n  - Sevenths: 7, maj7, m7, mMaj7, dim7, m7b5, 7#5\n  - Extensions: add9, 9, maj9, m9, 11, 13\nNotes are spelled by scale degree (Cm7 = C-Eb-G-Bb, C°7 = C-Eb-Gb-Bbb), not\nraw chromatics, so the labels teach correct theory. Voicings are octave-placed\nso even a 13th stays inside the C2..B6 keyboard.\n\nCovered by src/__tests__/chords.test.ts (root math, degree spelling, range).\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01J4JRpRUmttWRgFiWVUpbMk\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
